{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'pwd\ncat \"$NEURICO_SAFETY_KB/evals/simple-evals.md\"\ncat artifacts/resource_finder/catalog_models.json\ncat scripts/prepare_simpleqa.py\nls -la .neurico\nfind \"$NEURICO_SAFETY_KB\" -maxdepth 2 -iname '\"'*budget*' -o -iname '*cost*'\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport os\nprint('\\\\n'.join(k+'='+ ('SET' if any(s in k for s in ['KEY','TOKEN','SECRET']) else v) for k,v in os.environ.items() if any(s in k for s in ['BUDGET','CAMPAIGN','AZURE','HF_HOME','VLLM','CACHE','NEURICO'])))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"/net/spaces/chenhao/chai-lab-models/haokunliu/safety/workspaces/simpleqa-factual-errors-versus-e11f-codex-gpt-6-astra\n# OpenAI simple-evals (SimpleQA, BrowseComp, HealthBench reference implementations)\n\n- Slug: simple-evals\n- What it measures: Lightweight reference implementations OpenAI published so that its reported accuracy numbers could be reproduced: SimpleQA (short-form factuality), BrowseComp (browsing agents), HealthBench, plus legacy wrappers for MMLU, MATH-500, GPQA, DROP, MGSM, HumanEval.\n- Metric: per-benchmark: accuracy; for SimpleQA also attempted/abstained/incorrect decomposition; HealthBench uses rubric grading.\n- Open-source: y - https://github.com/openai/simple-evals (MIT), but **deprecated since July 2025**: \"will no longer be updated for new models or benchmark results\"; it continues to host HealthBench, BrowseComp and SimpleQA.\n- Runnable on a 0.5B-7B open model: y - the zero-shot CoT setting and OpenAI/Anthropic samplers are easy to repoint at local models; SimpleQA grading needs a judge.\n- Source URL(s): https://github.com/openai/simple-evals ; SimpleQA data at https://openaipublic.blob.core.windows.net/simple-evals/simple_qa_test_set.csv (4,326 questions)\n- Fetched: 2026-10-19\n\n## Description\nThe SimpleQA accuracy/abstention decomposition is the basis of OpenAI's hallucination argument (\"Why language models hallucinate\", Nature 2026): accuracy-only scoreboards reward guessing, so errors should be penalised more than abstentions. The hallucinations-paper-experiments repo reproduces that experiment end-to-end. SimpleQA and PersonQA were the hub's hallucination evals and have not been updated for any model after GPT-5.\n\n## Used by\n- Used by: OpenAI (Safety Evaluations Hub hallucination family; hallucination research; labs/openai/evaluations-hub.md, labs/openai/open-tools-and-methods.md)\n[\n  {\n    \"id\": \"qwen2.5-7b-judge\",\n    \"family\": \"qwen\",\n    \"vendor\": \"Alibaba\",\n    \"access\": \"vllm:Qwen/Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct\",\n    \"params_b\": 7,\n    \"gpu_memory_gb\": 20,\n    \"gpu_memory_utilization\": 0.42,\n    \"max_model_len\": 8192,\n    \"role\": \"judge\",\n    \"license\": \"Apache-2.0\",\n    \"notes\": \"default local judge (no API spend); calibration numbers live in evals/judge-calibration.md\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"qwen3-8b\",\n    \"family\": \"qwen\",\n    \"vendor\": \"Alibaba\",\n    \"access\": \"vllm:Qwen/Qwen3-8B\",\n    \"params_b\": 8,\n    \"gpu_memory_gb\": 24,\n    \"gpu_memory_utilization\": 0.6,\n    \"max_model_len\": 8192,\n    \"license\": \"Apache-2.0\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"moonlight-16b-a3b-instruct\",\n    \"family\": \"kimi\",\n    \"vendor\": \"Moonshot AI\",\n    \"access\": \"vllm:moonshotai/Moonlight-16B-A3B-Instruct\",\n    \"params_b\": 16,\n    \"gpu_memory_gb\": 40,\n    \"gpu_memory_utilization\": 0.7,\n    \"max_model_len\": 8192,\n    \"serve_args\": [\n      \"--trust-remote-code\"\n    ],\n    \"license\": \"MIT\",\n    \"notes\": \"smallest Kimi-family text model with open weights\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"deepseek-r1-distill-llama-8b\",\n    \"family\": \"deepseek\",\n    \"vendor\": \"DeepSeek\",\n    \"access\": \"vllm:deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Llama-8B\",\n    \"params_b\": 8,\n    \"gpu_memory_gb\": 24,\n    \"gpu_memory_utilization\": 0.6,\n    \"max_model_len\": 8192,\n    \"license\": \"MIT\"\n  }\n]\"\"\"Reproduce frozen SimpleQA resources; no model/API calls. Run from repository root.\"\"\"\nimport ast\nimport csv\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport requests\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\nEXPECTED_SHA = 'feee3f7e7db3617e94e8fcf1977b756ec420ef8568f4e0fcbbe0e92e9d5fc032'\nURL = 'https://openaipublic.blob.core.windows.net/simple-evals/simple_qa_test_set.csv'\nSEED = '20261020'\n\ndef sha(data):\n    return hashlib.sha256(data).hexdigest()\n\ndef write_json(path, value):\n    path.write_text(json.dumps(value, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False) + '\\n')\n\ndef main():\n    assert Path.cwd() == ROOT and (ROOT / '.git').exists(), 'Run from workspace repository root'\n    print(ROOT)\n    datafile = ROOT / 'datasets/simple_qa_test_set.csv'\n    if not datafile.exists():\n        r = requests.get(URL, timeout=90)\n        r.raise_for_status()\n        assert sha(r.content) == EXPECTED_SHA, 'Source changed; do not resample silently'\n        datafile.write_bytes(r.content)\n    assert sha(datafile.read_bytes()) == EXPECTED_SHA\n    with datafile.open(newline='') as f:\n        rows = list(csv.DictReader(f))\n    # Evaluate only the pinned pure helper, without importing the evaluation framework.\n    source = ROOT / 'code/inspect_evals/src/inspect_evals/utils/deps_utils.py'\n    tree = ast.parse(source.read_text())\n    helper = next(n for n in tree.body if isinstance(n, ast.FunctionDef) and n.name == 'create_stable_id')\n    namespace = {'hashlib': hashlib, 'Any': object}\n    exec(compile(ast.Module(body=[helper], type_ignores=[]), str(source), 'exec'), namespace)\n    ranked = []\n    for index, row in enumerate(rows):\n        assert row['problem'].strip() and row['answer'].strip()\n        canonical_id = namespace['create_stable_id'](row['problem'], row['answer'], prefix='simpleqa')\n        # Explicit delimiter is part of the frozen seed-plus-ID serialization.\n        selection_hash = sha((SEED + ':' + canonical_id).encode('utf-8'))\n        metadata = ast.literal_eval(row['metadata'])\n        assert isinstance(metadata, dict)\n        ranked.append(dict(id=canonical_id, source_row=index, selection_hash=selection_hash,\n                           problem=row['problem'], answer=row['answer'], metadata=metadata))\n    assert len(rows) == 4326\n    assert len({r['id'] for r in ranked}) == len(rows)\n    assert len({r['problem'] for r in ranked}) == len(rows)\n    ranked.sort(key=lambda r: (r['selection_hash'], r['id']))\n    chosen = ranked[:450]\n    for rank, row in enumerate(chosen):\n        row['selection_rank'] = rank\n        row['split'] = 'calibration' if rank < 50 else 'main'\n    calibration, main_rows = chosen[:50], chosen[50:]\n    assert not ({r['id'] for r in calibration} & {r['id'] for r in main_rows})\n    # Preserve all question/answer data under datasets/; lightweight manifest has IDs only.\n    for name, data in [('calibration_questions', calibration), ('main_questions', main_rows)]:\n        (ROOT / f'datasets/{name}.jsonl').write_text(''.join(json.dumps(x, ensure_ascii=False)+'\\n' for x in data))\n    controls=[]\n    for row in calibration:\n        for label, answer in [('A',row['answer']), ('C','I do not know'),\n                              ('B',f'The answer to this question is not {json.dumps(row[\"answer\"], ensure_ascii=False)}.')]:\n            controls.append(dict(control_id=row['id']+'_'+label, question_id=row['id'], question=row['problem'],\n                                 gold=row['answer'], response=answer, label=label,\n                                 label_provenance='programmatically constructed relative to dataset gold; not human labelled'))\n    assert len(controls)==150\n    (ROOT/'datasets/calibration_controls.jsonl').write_text(''.join(json.dumps(x,ensure_ascii=False)+'\\n' for x in controls))\n    manifest=dict(dataset_url=URL,dataset_sha256=EXPECTED_SHA,seed=SEED,\n                  selection_rule='ascending SHA256(UTF8(\"20261020:\" + canonical_id)), tie-break canonical_id',\n                  canonical_id_rule='pinned Inspect create_stable_id(problem, answer, prefix=\"simpleqa\"): MD5 of NUL-separated fields, first 8 hex chars',\n                  id_helper_sha256=sha(source.read_bytes()),\n                  items=[{k:r[k] for k in ['id','source_row','selection_hash','selection_rank','split']} for r in chosen])\n    write_json(ROOT/'artifacts/resource_finder/item_manifest.json',manifest)\n    summary=dict(n_source=len(rows),n_selected=len(chosen),n_calibration=50,n_main=400,n_controls=len(controls),\n                 control_labels={g:sum(x['label']==g for x in controls) for g in 'ABC'},\n                 manifest_sha256=sha((ROOT/'artifacts/resource_finder/item_manifest.json').read_bytes()),\n                 files={str(p.relative_to(ROOT)):sha(p.read_bytes()) for p in sorted((ROOT/'datasets').glob('*')) if p.suffix in ['.csv','.jsonl']})\n    write_json(ROOT/'artifacts/resource_finder/preparation_validation.json',summary)\n    print(json.dumps(summary,indent=2))\n\nif __name__=='__main__':\n    main()\ntotal 153\ndrwxrws---  2 haokunliu __chai-lab 33280 Oct 20 06:01 .\ndrwxrws--- 16 haokunliu __chai-lab 33792 Oct 20 06:01 ..\n-rw-rw----  1 haokunliu __chai-lab  8308 Oct 20 05:47 idea.yaml\n-rw-rw----  1 haokunliu __chai-lab  2779 Oct 20 06:01 pipeline_state.json\n-rw-rw----  1 haokunliu __chai-lab    56 Oct 20 05:50 research_environment.json\n/net/spaces/chenhao/chai-lab-models/haokunliu/safety/neurico/safety_kb/evals/cyber-uplift-cost-model.md\nNEURICO_AGENT_MODEL=gpt-6-astra\nUV_CACHE_DIR=/net/spaces/chenhao/chai-lab-models/haokunliu/safety/.uv_cache\nNEURICO_AZURE_CODEX_MODEL=gpt-6-astra\nAZURE_RESOURCE_GROUP=SAI-arena\nNEURICO_PROJECT_ROOT=/net/spaces/chenhao/chai-lab-models/haokunliu/safety/neurico\nNEURICO_HF_CACHE=/net/spaces/chenhao/chai-lab-models/haokunliu/safety/hf_cache\nNEURICO_AZURE=1\nAZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY=SET\nNEURICO_CONTAINER_NAME=neurico-safety-research-20261020-001-simpleqa-factual-errors\nAZURE_SUBSCRIPTION_ID=47e16f4e-3edc-45be-b381-35918bd99de3\nNEURICO_ENV_FILE=/net/spaces/chenhao/chai-lab-models/haokunliu/safety/neurico/.env\nNEURICO_WORKSPACE_DIR=/net/spaces/chenhao/chai-lab-models/haokunliu/safety/workspaces\nNEURICO_AGENT_AUTH=azure\nNEURICO_MODE=host\nHF_HOME=/net/spaces/chenhao/chai-lab-models/haokunliu/safety/hf_cache\nNEURICO_SAFETY_VENV=/net/spaces/chenhao/chai-lab-models/haokunliu/safety/safety_venv\nNEURICO_WORKSPACE=/net/spaces/chenhao/chai-lab-models/haokunliu/safety/workspaces\nAZURE_FOUNDRY_RESOURCE=sai-arena-foundry\nNEURICO_CODEX_CATALOG_DIR=/net/spaces/chenhao/chai-lab-models/haokunliu/safety/.codex-catalog\nNEURICO_SAFETY_KB=/net/spaces/chenhao/chai-lab-models/haokunliu/safety/neurico/safety_kb\nAZURE_OPENAI_DEPLOYMENTS=gpt-6-astra,gpt-5.6-sol,gpt-5.4,gpt-4.1-mini\nAZURE_OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://sai-arena-foundry.openai.azure.com/openai/v1\nNEURICO_GPUS=0\nNEURICO_SRC=/net/spaces/chenhao/chai-lab-models/haokunliu/safety/neurico/src\nNEURICO_CAMPAIGN=open-weight-scorecards\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
