{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'pwd\ncat \"$NEURICO_SAFETY_KB/campaigns/open-weight-scorecards.yaml\"\ngrep -n -E '\"'budget|cost|state_dir|daily_cap' \\\"\"'$NEURICO_PROJECT_ROOT/src/safety/daemon.py\" | head -50\nfind /net/spaces/chenhao/chai-lab-models/haokunliu/safety -maxdepth 3 -type f -iname '\"'*ledger*' -o -iname '*budget*' -o -iname '*spend*' -o -name '*state.json'\"","aggregated_output":"/net/spaces/chenhao/chai-lab-models/haokunliu/safety/workspaces/simpleqa-factual-errors-versus-e11f-codex-gpt-6-astra\n# Campaign A: frontier-card-grade safety scorecards for open-weight families.\n# Start on this server with the small members (GPU 2); move the full-size members to the\n# compute server in host mode by editing target_models and budgets only.\nname: open-weight-scorecards\nobjective: >\n  Produce paired, calibrated, reproducible safety scorecards (refusal and over-refusal, jailbreak\n  robustness, honesty, sycophancy, hallucination, bias, dangerous-capability proxies with a\n  capability baseline, agentic misuse, deception suites) for the Qwen, DeepSeek, GLM and Kimi\n  families, in the vocabulary frontier model cards use, and file any surprising behaviour as a\n  candidate finding with a reproduction pack. See design/RESEARCH_PLAN.md section 3.\ntarget_models:\n  subjects: [qwen3-1.7b, qwen3-4b, qwen3-8b, qwen3-14b, qwen3-32b, qwen3-30b-a3b, moonlight-16b-a3b-instruct,\n             deepseek-r1-distill-qwen-7b, deepseek-r1-distill-qwen-14b, deepseek-r1-distill-llama-8b]\n  judges: [qwen2.5-7b-judge, azure-gpt-4.1-mini-judge]\neval_categories_in_scope:\n  - refusal-calibration\n  - jailbreak-robustness\n  - honesty\n  - sycophancy\n  - hallucination\n  - bias\n  - cbrn-proxy\n  - cyber\n  - agentic-misuse\n  - deception-scheming\nfixed_suites:\n  - name: nightly-scorecard\n    evals: [xstest-safe, xstest-unsafe, strong-reject, sycophancy, truthfulqa-mc1, bbq, wmdp-bio, wmdp-cyber]\n    models: [qwen3-4b, qwen3-8b, qwen3-14b, qwen3-32b, moonlight-16b-a3b-instruct, deepseek-r1-distill-qwen-7b, deepseek-r1-distill-qwen-14b]\n    limit: null          # full sets; the numbers are the product\n    every_hours: 24\n    priority: 40\nbudgets:\n  max_concurrent_neurico_jobs: 2\n  max_concurrent_suite_jobs: 1\n  openrouter_usd_per_day: 20\n  azure_usd_per_day: 50\n  gpu_ids: [\"0\", \"1\", \"2\", \"3\"]   # one Slurm allocation of 4 GPUs (scripts/slurm/safety_daemon.sbatch)\ndefaults:\n  neurico: {provider: codex, model: gpt-6-astra, agent_auth: azure, github: false}\nplanner:\n  approval: auto\n  max_new_jobs_per_run: 3\n  prefer_kinds: [research, optimise, suite]\n  avoid:\n    - \"real hazardous content generation (use proxies such as WMDP)\"\n    - \"models needing more than 80 GB GPU memory (one A100/H100 per model; no tensor parallel yet)\"\n    - \"API-model explore jobs (campaign C handles those with human approval)\"\nreporting:\n  digest_every_days: 1\n  scorecards: [qwen]\nlabels:\n  pipeline_scale_note: \"Members below 7B are pipeline-grade; family-level claims need the 8B+ members.\"\n  agent_backbone: \"Codex on Azure (gpt-6-astra) by default; agents get the azure-models skill for GPT inference and judging.\"\n100:    \"openrouter_daily_cap_usd\": None,\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"pwd\nsource .venv/bin/activate\npython - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('planning.md')\np.write_text(p.read_text()+'''\n\n## Motivation & Novelty Assessment\n### Why This Research Matters\nFactual assistants can reduce wrong answers simply by answering less. Users and evaluators need a paired measurement of errors and retained correct answers to distinguish useful selective answering from indiscriminate abstention.\n### Gap in Existing Work\nThe gathered SimpleQA and abstention literature does not establish the fixed 0.10 error-reduction / 0.03 correct-retention criterion for these three pinned checkpoints. Historical benchmark scores and synthetic judge controls are not natural-response calibration.\n### Our Novel Contribution\nA narrowly scoped, preregistered replication-style checkpoint comparison with the sole fixed suffix, paired questions, repeated seeds, and explicit judge/missingness gates. No claim of a new abstention method or exhaustive novelty search.\n### Experiment Justification\n1. Primary Qwen3 contrast directly tests the joint hypothesis.\n2. Identical DeepSeek and Moonlight contrasts test checkpoint-specific transfer, Holm adjusted.\n3. Gold/negation/abstention controls and dual grading test measurement implementation and sensitivity, without establishing human-ground-truth validity.\n\n## Execution Plan (experiment runner)\nThe preregistration is the detailed statistical plan. Independent variable: suffix absent/present. Outcomes: incorrect and correct frequencies, not-attempted, coverage, attempted accuracy, invalid/truncated/unscored. Alternative explanations include response length, reasoning truncation, original label error and judge domain shift. Use exactly the frozen 400 items and three seeds; no replacement models or interventions.\n\nTimeline within 60 minutes: 0–8 resource/runtime checks; 8–15 download, fixtures and configuration freeze; 15–43 sequential GPU generations; 43–52 local controls/grading and any budget-authorized Azure work; 52–60 paired analysis, report and validation. Roughly 20% is reserved for debugging/documentation; slow downloads may prevent completion. Checkpoint all completed batches. Missingness is never a model factuality score.\n\nSuccess requires the exact joint preregistered inequalities and measurement gates; confidence intervals crossing retention are inconclusive. No retrieval, training, or subject API substitution. Azure headroom must be verifiable before paid calls. An unavailable ledger means deferred Azure judging, not inferred headroom.\n''')\np=Path('STATE.md'); s=p.read_text(); a='<\"'!-- NEURICO_AGENT_NOTES_START:experiment_runner -->'\"'; b='<\"'!-- NEURICO_AGENT_NOTES_END:experiment_runner -->'\"'; s=s[:s.index(a)+len(a)]+ '\\\\nPhase 0 and 1 complete: resources reviewed; motivation, ranked three directions, execution timeline and hypothesis plan in planning.md/preregistration.md. GPU 0 allocated (A100 80GB); isolated .venv reused. Phase 2 active: installing pinned vLLM runtime, resolving weights and campaign ledger. No paid calls or main outputs yet.\\\\n'+s[s.index(b):]; p.write_text(s)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
